INDEPENDENT VARIABLES 
 
#  The original data are available for center of mass energies 1.e-1 to 
#  100 eV. The reduced mass for the system is ra_mass, in the reactions
#  list below.  The cross section specific energy range is obtained by
#  dividing the c-of-m range by ra_mass (in AMU). The specific energy
#  range for the integrals is the c-of-m range divided by the test
#  species mass (in AMU). Likewise, divide by the background species mass
#  to get the specific temperature range. However, to get adequate 
#  accuracy in the integrals and moment expressions, we utilize the
#  extrapolations in the cross section fits to lower energies and 
#  actually use a minimum energy of 1.e-3 here.  With no such extrapolation
#  available for the scattering angle, these remain at the original
#  range and otherwise match those of the cross section.

#  Independent          Min.                 Max.             No. of   Spacing
#  Variable                                                   Values

1
specific_energy       1.98501189902709e-03   198.501189902709     101     log
2 3 4 5  
specific_energy       9.92235755215439e-04   99.2235755215439      51     log
2 3 4 5 
specific_temperature  9.92776143811646e-04   99.2776143811646      51     log 
6
1st_random_number     0.	             1. 	          251     linear
6
specific_energy       1.98501189902709e-01   198.501189902709      31     log

